Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses feedback from Minemine (linux.do) on multi-user isolation design.

When the same user accesses Hermes from different channels (CLI, Telegram,
Discord), each channel gets a separate memory directory (memories/{chat_id}/).
This script unifies them via symlinks:

- memories/{chat_id}/ → memories/user_{username}/
- Global MEMORY.md/USER.md → user's directory (for CLI sessions)
- Different users remain isolated (per PR #17989)

Commands: map, unmap, list, resolve, migrate
Pure filesystem solution — no Hermes code changes needed.

Companion to PR #17989 (per-user isolation):
- #17989: isolates different users
- This: unifies same user across channels
